al\": \"Sony's DRM software secretly 'phones home' when CDs are played, a behavior hid\", \"rephrased\": \"Sony's digital rights management software secretly transmits data to the company's servers every time a CD is played, a behavior that is explicitly concealed from the license agreement and the rootkit itself. This hidden surveillance capability raises significant concerns among media rights activists and artists regarding privacy and consent, as users are unaware that their usage patterns are being monitored without their knowledge.\", \"summary\": \"Sony's DRM software secretly monitors CD usage in a way hidden from the license agreement and users.\"}}",
